-- NPI, DEA_NUMBER, and MBI filters. First-class entity types for three U.S.
-- healthcare identifiers, so they are labelled npi, dea-number, and mbi rather
-- than as custom identifiers, with no pattern for the policy author to write.
-- NPI: ten digits beginning with 1 or 2 that pass the NPI check digit (the Luhn
-- check of the number with the 80840 prefix), e.g. 1234567893. DEA_NUMBER: two
-- letters, or a letter and 9, followed by seven digits that pass the DEA check
-- digit, e.g. AB1234563. MBI: the eleven-character Medicare Beneficiary
-- Identifier in the format CMS publishes, e.g. 1EG4-TE5-MK73. None has options.
-- Added to schema 1.3.0 in place (additive). Compiles to clinical-identifiers.json.

POLICY clinical_identifiers;

REDACT NPI WITH LAST_4;
REDACT DEA_NUMBER WITH MASK;
REDACT MBI WITH REDACT;
